// Bun Snapshot v1, https://bun.sh/docs/test/snapshots

exports[`frozen CLI descriptor and help graph snapshots root, every group, and every command help form 1`] = `
"Usage
  explodex [GLOBAL OPTIONS] <GROUP> <COMMAND> [ARGUMENTS] [OPTIONS]
  explodex help [GROUP [COMMAND ...]]

Description
  Explodex manages trusted plugins for the installed read-only
  /Applications/ChatGPT.app with bounded one-shot operations.

  Explodex runs no daemon and never automatically restarts, reloads,
  navigates, closes, or stops an existing authoring main.

Groups
  host            Read-only ChatGPT.app identity and host evidence.
  compatibility   Exact compatibility key status.
  main            Authoring-main classification and final apply.
  plugin          Plugin authoring, artifacts, lifecycle, and registry operations.
  dev             One persistent isolated development instance on 127.0.0.1:9444.

Global options
  -h, --help
      Show help for the selected path and exit.
  -V, --version
      Print the CLI version and exit.
      --json
      Emit one schemaVersion-1 JSON envelope on stdout.
      --home <path>
      Override the Explodex home directory. (default: $HOME/.explodex)
      --dev-root <path>
      Override the isolated development root. (default: <home>/dev/plugin-dev)
      --timeout <duration>
      Application-level bound for the operation (for example 60s).
      --no-color
      Disable ANSI color even on a TTY.

Environment
  EXPLODEX_HOME       Default Explodex home ($HOME/.explodex)
  EXPLODEX_DEV_ROOT   Default development root (<home>/dev/plugin-dev)
  NO_COLOR            Disable color when present
  TERM=dumb           Disable color and terminal decoration

Compatibility
  Host: read-only /Applications/ChatGPT.app only.
  Ports: main 127.0.0.1:9333, isolated development 127.0.0.1:9444.
  Inspect compatibility with: explodex compatibility status

Main recovery
  Explodex never automatically restarts or debug-relaunches an existing authoring main.
  Provide a manual debug-enabled main on 127.0.0.1:9333, then use
  explodex main apply <artifact> only after isolated-dev validation.

Examples
  explodex host report
  explodex --json compatibility status
  explodex help plugin

More information
  explodex help <group>
  explodex <group> <command> --help
"
`;

